    "s01": { "translation": "Brothers, all of us who were baptized into Christ Jesus were baptized into His death. For we were buried with Him through baptism into death, so that, just as Christ rose from the dead through the glory of the Father, we too might walk in newness of life. For if we have become united with Him in the likeness of His death, we will also be united with Him in the likeness of His resurrection. We know this: our old self was crucified with Him so that the body of sin might be destroyed and we might no longer serve sin. For whoever has died has been freed from sin. But if we have died with Christ, we believe that we will also live together with Christ, knowing that Christ, risen from the dead, no longer dies, and death will no longer rule over Him. For the death He died, He died to sin once for all, but the life He lives, He lives to God. So you too must consider yourselves dead to sin, but alive to God in Christ Jesus our Lord.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w003", "w004"], "anchor": "w003", "gloss": "were baptized" }, { "words": ["w009", "w010"], "anchor": "w009", "gloss": "His death" }, { "words": ["w011", "w012"], "anchor": "w011", "gloss": "were baptized" }, { "words": ["w013", "w014", "w015"], "anchor": "w013", "gloss": "for we were buried together" }, { "words": ["w032", "w033"], "anchor": "w033", "gloss": "we too" }, { "words": ["w034", "w035", "w036", "w037"], "anchor": "w037", "gloss": "might walk in newness of life" }, { "words": ["w038", "w039"], "anchor": "w039", "gloss": "for if" }, { "words": ["w040", "w041", "w042"], "anchor": "w040", "gloss": "we have been planted together" }, { "words": ["w044", "w045"], "anchor": "w044", "gloss": "of His death" }, { "words": ["w046", "w047", "w048", "w049"], "anchor": "w049", "gloss": "we will also be united in the likeness of His resurrection" }, { "words": ["w050", "w051", "w052"], "anchor": "w051", "gloss": "we know this:" }, { "words": ["w053", "w054", "w055"], "anchor": "w054", "gloss": 